{"schemaVersion":1,"storyId":"the-frogs-who-sang-too-loud","version":1,"title":"The Frogs Who Sang Too Loud","ageTiers":["7-8","9-10"],"language":"en","narrationLocale":"en-GH","pages":[{"n":1,"text":"It was the rainy season. Behind Atsu’s house, there was a pond, and in the pond lived a hundred frogs. Every night they sang, ‘Ribbit! Ribbit! Ribbit!’ Atsu could not sleep.","sentences":["It was the rainy season.","Behind Atsu’s house, there was a pond, and in the pond lived a hundred frogs.","Every night they sang, ‘Ribbit!","Ribbit!","Ribbit!’ Atsu could not sleep."],"alt":"A boy lies in bed with a pillow over his head while frogs sing outside.","image":{"hash":"sha256:4f0b7257343ea6e1f857cbee06cd91751a141a680639135b739ef5af61364e13","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:dad664e1e6a51f73596a9c72ec3f559d3127db1bff048fc73d159ae9afe75c1c","durationMs":20000,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,2865],[2865,11303],[11303,15019],[15019,16206],[16206,20000]],"words":[[0,258],[258,645],[645,1032],[1032,1677],[1677,2865],[2865,3639],[3639,4284],[4284,5135],[5135,5781],[5781,6168],[6168,6297],[6297,7019],[7019,7406],[7406,7665],[7665,8052],[8052,8568],[8568,9213],[9213,9342],[9342,10245],[10245,11303],[11303,11948],[11948,12594],[12594,13110],[13110,13832],[13832,15019],[15019,16206],[16206,17394],[17394,17910],[17910,18555],[18555,18942],[18942,20000]]}}},{"n":2,"text":"Atsu put cotton in his ears. It did not help. ‘Those frogs sing too loud!’ he groaned. ‘Tomorrow, I will chase them all away.’","sentences":["Atsu put cotton in his ears.","It did not help.","‘Those frogs sing too loud!’ he groaned.","‘Tomorrow, I will chase them all away.’"],"alt":"A boy with cotton in his ears frowns at the window.","image":{"hash":"sha256:0efb95c91870c038c929236f06c9c653870a9077905cbe4f422dc4de3458dfa5","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:7b7e61f5c2a36093a32f901bec7021b9032d349ad8e515817c866b546205d46d","durationMs":13680,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,3117],[3117,4997],[4997,9499],[9499,13680]],"words":[[0,495],[495,866],[866,1608],[1608,1855],[1855,2226],[2226,3117],[3117,3364],[3364,3735],[3735,4106],[4106,4997],[4997,5615],[5615,6234],[6234,6729],[6729,7100],[7100,7990],[7990,8238],[8238,9499],[9499,10687],[10687,10810],[10810,11305],[11305,11924],[11924,12418],[12418,12789],[12789,13680]]}}},{"n":3,"text":"In the morning, Grandma Korkoi laughed. ‘Do not chase them,’ she said. ‘The boy frogs are singing to call the girl frogs. And a loud pond is a healthy pond.’ ‘Healthy?’ said Atsu.","sentences":["In the morning, Grandma Korkoi laughed.","‘Do not chase them,’ she said.","‘The boy frogs are singing to call the girl frogs.","And a loud pond is a healthy pond.’ ‘Healthy?’ said Atsu."],"alt":"A grandmother smiles at her grandson on the porch.","image":{"hash":"sha256:1840a1032ad0b714aaec5657539e102dbefef1966c9a230b1ad74f228b14f2df","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:b1048af91b6c31856c0e67482b6c0c6aa729ebc14a1110b24694d799c1e214dd","durationMs":18720,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,4433],[4433,7541],[7541,12625],[12625,18720]],"words":[[0,241],[241,602],[602,1638],[1638,2482],[2482,3204],[3204,4433],[4433,4674],[4674,5035],[5035,5638],[5638,6312],[6312,6674],[6674,7541],[7541,7902],[7902,8264],[8264,8866],[8866,9227],[9227,10071],[10071,10312],[10312,10794],[10794,11155],[11155,11637],[11637,12625],[12625,12986],[12986,13106],[13106,13588],[13588,14070],[14070,14311],[14311,14432],[14432,15275],[15275,16142],[16142,17371],[17371,17853],[17853,18720]]}}},{"n":4,"text":"‘Frogs eat insects, including mosquitoes,’ said Grandma. ‘And a frog has thin, soft skin that takes in water and air. So it needs clean water to live. When the water is spoiled, frogs go away.’","sentences":["‘Frogs eat insects, including mosquitoes,’ said Grandma.","‘And a frog has thin, soft skin that takes in water and air.","So it needs clean water to live.","When the water is spoiled, frogs go away.’"],"alt":"A frog catches a mosquito with its tongue beside a clean pond.","image":{"hash":"sha256:f83a37da28a160e3fcc25216b82b7c40abaeba0c8b384f6b31d3ece66f4b20dc","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:39d16232fad846d4007d9faf4cf7b1a7a0aa809e75c8c9253d975c339638450a","durationMs":18040,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,5579],[5579,10985],[10985,14046],[14046,18040]],"words":[[0,543],[543,868],[868,1802],[1802,2779],[2779,4038],[4038,4472],[4472,5579],[5579,5905],[5905,6013],[6013,6448],[6448,6773],[6773,7381],[7381,7815],[7815,8249],[8249,8684],[8684,9226],[9226,9443],[9443,9986],[9986,10312],[10312,10985],[10985,11202],[11202,11419],[11419,11962],[11962,12504],[12504,13047],[13047,13264],[13264,14046],[14046,14480],[14480,14805],[14805,15348],[15348,15565],[15565,16499],[16499,17041],[17041,17258],[17258,18040]]}}},{"n":5,"text":"A few weeks later, some people threw plastic bags and old bottles near the pond. Mud and rubbish drifted in. The water turned dull and smelly.","sentences":["A few weeks later, some people threw plastic bags and old bottles near the pond.","Mud and rubbish drifted in.","The water turned dull and smelly."],"alt":"Plastic bags and bottles lie at the edge of a muddy pond.","image":{"hash":"sha256:5c38bc303c786dc622dd0723bfcde343b4da58bba011db836fee5e98aab3e615","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:13e73a2212c861c40f35880fc7f8fcde0f1e1e1b86d0e4f919ff4ba897e14b8d","durationMs":18560,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,10281],[10281,14047],[14047,18560]],"words":[[0,149],[149,598],[598,1345],[1345,2331],[2331,2929],[2929,3826],[3826,4573],[4573,5619],[5619,6217],[6217,6665],[6665,7113],[7113,8159],[8159,8757],[8757,9205],[9205,10281],[10281,10730],[10730,11178],[11178,12224],[12224,13270],[13270,14047],[14047,14495],[14495,15243],[15243,16139],[16139,16737],[16737,17185],[17185,18560]]}}},{"n":6,"text":"That night, there was no ribbit. No song at all. The house was very quiet. But Atsu still could not sleep. Instead, he heard, ‘Zzzzz!’ Mosquitoes!","sentences":["That night, there was no ribbit.","No song at all.","The house was very quiet.","But Atsu still could not sleep.","Instead, he heard, ‘Zzzzz!’ Mosquitoes!"],"alt":"A boy lies awake in a quiet room, with a mosquito buzzing near his ear.","image":{"hash":"sha256:df53e84158f76749c523e4286abcf992606da50ebef2b11b82f3f0324636fb25","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:1960fe061223e36b4c489ec3e6af08060f47220ee3c88613411218fa84c1f130","durationMs":20840,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,4635],[4635,6843],[6843,10451],[10451,14837],[14837,20840]],"words":[[0,622],[622,1649],[1649,2426],[2426,2893],[2893,3204],[3204,4635],[4635,4946],[4946,5568],[5568,5879],[5879,6843],[6843,7310],[7310,8087],[8087,8554],[8554,9176],[9176,10451],[10451,10918],[10918,11540],[11540,12317],[12317,13095],[13095,13562],[13562,14837],[14837,16174],[16174,16485],[16485,17512],[17512,18787],[18787,20840]]}}},{"n":7,"text":"‘I miss the frogs,’ said Atsu. ‘So let us help them,’ said Grandma. With gloves and a sack, and with two grown-ups watching, Atsu and his cousins picked up the rubbish from the edge. They did not go into the water.","sentences":["‘I miss the frogs,’ said Atsu.","‘So let us help them,’ said Grandma.","With gloves and a sack, and with two grown-ups watching, Atsu and his cousins picked up the rubbish from the edge.","They did not go into the water."],"alt":"Children in gloves put rubbish into a sack at the edge of a pond while adults watch.","image":{"hash":"sha256:d7c7badc9f4005b62ca71a9a65532207200d5dc79f36f730d9df91284b1a1606","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:562f9e34ecefd5991097285f60ef4078e216b232acfa637a36d3f8ceafc5b051","durationMs":25240,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,3614],[3614,7928],[7928,21430],[21430,25240]],"words":[[0,140],[140,700],[700,1121],[1121,2045],[2045,2605],[2605,3614],[3614,3894],[3894,4314],[4314,4594],[4594,5154],[5154,5939],[5939,6499],[6499,7928],[7928,8488],[8488,9328],[9328,9749],[9749,9889],[9889,10673],[10673,11093],[11093,11654],[11654,12074],[12074,13194],[13194,14539],[14539,15099],[15099,15519],[15519,15940],[15940,16920],[16920,17760],[17760,18041],[18041,18461],[18461,19441],[19441,20002],[20002,20422],[20422,21430],[21430,21990],[21990,22411],[22411,22831],[22831,23111],[23111,23671],[23671,24091],[24091,25240]]}}},{"n":8,"text":"Months later, the rains came back, and the pond filled with clean water. One night, Atsu heard it again: ‘Ribbit! Ribbit!’ He smiled and slept like a log. The end.","sentences":["Months later, the rains came back, and the pond filled with clean water.","One night, Atsu heard it again: ‘Ribbit!","Ribbit!’ He smiled and slept like a log.","The end."],"alt":"A boy sleeps happily while frogs sing in a clean pond outside.","image":{"hash":"sha256:c499a27c091a2637428b960d23bdf85301b23fde73602854870bf9dafa866315","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:2e696bfe10b660b2dfcce765b100c5c7e9742e5b44bee86787804e809a7621fd","durationMs":20160,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,8791],[8791,13837],[13837,18884],[18884,20160]],"words":[[0,832],[832,1747],[1747,2163],[2163,2856],[2856,3411],[3411,4187],[4187,4603],[4603,5019],[5019,5574],[5574,6406],[6406,6960],[6960,7654],[7654,8791],[8791,9206],[9206,10122],[10122,10676],[10676,11369],[11369,11647],[11647,12562],[12562,13837],[13837,15113],[15113,15390],[15390,16222],[16222,16638],[16638,17331],[17331,17886],[17886,18025],[18025,18884],[18884,19300],[19300,20160]]}}}],"activities":[{"id":"frog-c1","type":"comprehension","afterPage":3,"question":"Why do the boy frogs sing?","options":["To call the girl frogs","To scare Atsu","To ask for food"],"correctIndex":0},{"id":"frog-c2","type":"comprehension","afterPage":4,"question":"Why do frogs need clean water?","options":["Their thin skin takes in water and air","They like bubbles","They dislike mud only"],"correctIndex":0},{"id":"frog-ph","type":"phonics","afterPage":6,"targetSound":"fr","prompt":"Which words start with the fr sound, like frog?","options":["frog","fish","from","pond"],"correctIndexes":[0,2]},{"id":"frog-p1","type":"prediction","afterPage":7,"prompt":"Atsu and the grown-ups clean the rubbish. What might the frogs do? Tell a friend.","options":["Come back when the water is clean","Never come back"]},{"id":"frog-s1","type":"sequencing","prompt":"Put the story in order.","items":["Atsu wants the frogs to be quiet.","Grandma tells him about frogs and clean water.","The pond is spoiled and the frogs go quiet.","Atsu helps clean the edge and the frogs return."]},{"id":"frog-sel","type":"sel","afterPage":8,"prompt":"Atsu missed the frogs when they were gone. How do you feel when something you took for granted goes away?","feelingOptions":["Sad","Thoughtful","Thankful","Determined"]}],"glossary":[{"word":"pond","definition":"A small area of still water.","pages":[1,5]},{"word":"mosquitoes","definition":"Small flying insects that bite and can spread illness.","pages":[4,6]},{"word":"healthy","definition":"Well and strong, not ill.","pages":[3]},{"word":"rubbish","definition":"Things that people throw away.","pages":[5,7]}],"assets":{"sha256:4f0b7257343ea6e1f857cbee06cd91751a141a680639135b739ef5af61364e13":{"path":"/story-spark-preview/candidates/the-frogs-who-sang-too-loud/page1-1.webp","bytes":117854,"type":"image/webp"},"sha256:dad664e1e6a51f73596a9c72ec3f559d3127db1bff048fc73d159ae9afe75c1c":{"path":"/story-spark-preview/audio/dad664e1e6a5.mp3","bytes":160748,"type":"audio/mpeg"},"sha256:0efb95c91870c038c929236f06c9c653870a9077905cbe4f422dc4de3458dfa5":{"path":"/story-spark-preview/candidates/the-frogs-who-sang-too-l